cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ARBITER in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ARBITER: Unified attack attribution for teleportation-based quantum digital signatures"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Team F0rg3d (SIH26-A0H-T043)"
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ROHIT-JR/ARBITER"
abstract: >-
  A simulation and detection framework for teleportation-based quantum digital
  signatures. A single Neyman-Pearson generalized likelihood-ratio test, with
  likelihoods derived from density-matrix models and cross-checked against Qiskit
  circuits, detects and attributes forgery, impersonation, replay and
  quantum-channel manipulation. It is complemented by an anytime-valid sequential
  test, a CHSH channel-integrity check, quantum Chernoff performance bounds, and a
  hash-chained audit ledger dual-signed with ML-DSA-65 and a Merkle-Lamport
  hash-based signature. Developed for Smart India Hackathon 2026, PS 26141
  (Egreen Quanta).
keywords:
  - quantum digital signatures
  - quantum teleportation
  - hypothesis testing
  - quantum Chernoff bound
  - CHSH
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - Qiskit
